To apply a Gaussian filter before Sobel edge detection, you can add a few lines of code after loading the input image. Here's how:

```matlab
% Load input image
input_image = imread('image.jpg');

% Convert to grayscale
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);

% Define parameters for Gaussian filter
sigma = 1; % Standard deviation of Gaussian kernel
size = floor([5 5] * (sigma * sqrt(2 * log(10))) + 1); % Size of Gaussian kernel based on sigma

% Generate Gaussian kernel
[gaussian, x, y] = fspecial('gaussian', size, sigma);

% Apply Gaussian filter
filtered_image = filter2(gaussian, gray_image, 'replicate');

% Define Sobel operators
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];

% Apply Sobel operator in x direction
edge_image_x = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_x, 'same');

% Apply Sobel operator in y direction
edge_image_y = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');

% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);

% Display edge image
imshow(edge_image);
```

